SUMMARY:Olio Family Vacay Guatemala: From Antigua to Lake Atitlán
DESCRIPTION:OlioTrips are open to everyone and we foster the spirit of mean
 ingful connections\, new experiences and a space where you can be at ease.
  Think family vacation but with a chosen family (and without the bickering
  😂). In 2024\, Antigua became an extension of the Olio ecosystem.That y
 ear we spent a month in Guatemala running two OlioTrips\, and our favorite
  part (besides swimming in Lake Atitlán) was how our group got the chance
  to connect and bond with locals: the artists\, musicians\, business owner
 s\, and teachers we met along the way\, the house parties and homestyle di
 nners we were welcomed into.We're tied in with friends who run venues and 
 community projects similar to Olio\, and we've stayed in touch since the l
 ast trip. Those friends are onto all kinds of new projects\, and they've t
 old us that when we come back\, this trip will be even better than the las
 t.Nothing leaves us more recharged and inspired than time in Antigua\, fol
 lowed by the quiet integration that Lake Atitlán offers. Our last trip th
 ere is what inspired us to open our own venue\, and we think it's time tha
 t Olio goes back to Guatemala.Our dear friend\, Mayte Oliva\, cultural pro
 ducer\, photographer\, designer\, and all-around lovely human being\, will
  be with us for the entirety of the trip. She'll welcome and guide us thro
 ugh experiences that we would never see on our own\, and have us belly lau
 ghing throughout.Flow of the trip: Antigua - Jan 15 - 19thThis time\, we'r
 e settling into a gorgeous home in Antigua for the first half of the trip.
  Days are for workshops at our friend’s artist residency\, chef-prepared
  meals in a local architect’s orchid garden\, or wandering the dreamy st
 reets of this UNESCO-listed town\; nights are for inviting artists and loc
 als over for dinners\, dancing\, renting out the local movie theater\, sal
 ons\, and intimate house concerts.Lake Atitlan - Jan 19th - 22ndThen we mo
 ve to the lake\, where the pace slows even further. Some of us will relax 
 and take it all in\; others will join a sunrise hike or a cooking workshop
 . Either way\, we'll share meals\, play games\, and make a new group of be
 st friends before heading home restored.Selfishly\, we can't wait to go ba
 ck and we can't wait to share this world with you: swimming through the he
 at of the day\, visiting our friends' studios and restaurants\, and baskin
 g in new friendships as artists and teachers we love come to us for house 
 concerts and shared meals.We've built this trip to move slowly so that we 
 come home recharged and inspired. Welcome to Guatemala!&nbsp\;--Full price
  for the 8 day trip: Shared room $2750. Private Room $3350. Duo $5\,300 fo
 r two\, or ($2\,650/person)$500 deposit to reserve your spot!Balance to be
  paid in full by Dec 1.Reach out for payment plan options. Included:Accomm
 odations (7 nights)All breakfasts + 5 additional mealsMajority of workshop
 s\, tours\, and activitiesTransportation to/from activitiesTips for driver
 s &amp\; guides Not Included:Flights to/from GuatemalaMeals not listedTrav
 el insurancePersonal expenses---What kind of traveler is this trip for?Thi
 s trip is for people who want to experience Guatemala as if they were visi
 ting a local friend. You want to see places and meet people that would pro
 bably never happen were you to go on your own. All of our guides and frien
 ds in Antigua speak English\, so language wont be a barrier - but if you d
 o speak Spanish all the better!This is the right trip if you:Enjoy the ble
 nd of curiosity and social life that defines an Olio. Workshops and wander
 ing by day\, dinners\, salons and house concerts by night.Are drawn to Ant
 igua's mix of colonial streets\, artist studios\, and creative community.W
 ant a good amount of unstructured time built in and not just a packed itin
 erary. Space to wander\, rest by the lake\, linger at a long lunch or foll
 ow a conversation wherever it goes.Enjoy small groups where you'll actuall
 y get to know everyone by the end. That’s why we call it a family vacay!
 This trip works well whether you're coming solo or with a friend. Most Oli
 o travelers come alone\, and the group itself becomes the reason you’ll 
 want to come on the next trip!In their own words\, travelers from our last
  Guatemala trip:"Amigos\, before I get back into my New York flow: Thank y
 ou so much for such a beautiful trip. It fulfilled so much of what I want 
 all the time but especially what I need right now—time outside (and in t
 he water\, swoon)\; with people who are lovely and interesting who can tak
 e me out of my world\; and getting out of my head and into joy\, sun\, and
  community."- Pilar"Thanks to the Olio team for organizing\, guiding\, and
  supporting us during the trip! Thanks to everyone for the meaningful and 
 fun conversations as well. This trip surpassed every expectation I had\, a
 llowed me to fully pause my work life\, validate things I've been thinking
  about\, generate new work and non-work ideas\, and enjoy and learn about 
 everything we did."- Ritesh"Shoutout to @think.olio and a very special gro
 up of people who provided me the space to experience and be witness to lov
 e\, care\, connection\, joy\, vulnerability\, humility\, healing\, wonder\
 , and so much goddamn fun. I was inspired by the resistance\, resiliency a
 nd ancestral veneration as a daily practice. This trip was a beautiful lif
 e lesson in showing up\, and letting life surprise you."- NicoleAccommodat
 ions(Think boutique accommodations - not luxury but definitely grown up an
 d very comfortable)Antigua: We'll be based at two gorgeous properties that
  are an attraction in themselves and also an easy walk into Antigua's UNES
 CO-listed streets.Lake Atitlán: We move to our accommodations right on th
 e lake with gardens\, hammocks\, a pool\, kayaks\, and a private organic g
 arden and meals.How rooming works:Shared Room ($2\,750) — You'll room wi
 th another Olio traveler. If you're coming solo\, we'll match you thoughtf
 ully (most of our travelers come this way).Private Room ($3\,350) — Your
  own room for the whole trip\, subject to availability.Duo ($5\,300 for tw
 o\, or $2\,650/person) — Coming with a friend or partner? Book together 
 and each save $100 off the shared rate. We’ll have options to share a be
 d or to have separate beds in a shared room.Room availability at both prop
 erties is limited\, so we recommend booking early\, especially if you're s
 et on a private room.\n\nTickets & info: https://www.viewcy.com/event/olio
 trip_guatemala_o
URL:https://www.viewcy.com/event/oliotrip_guatemala_o
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
